  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1250 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nAn omega block will continue to provide tranquil weather conditions \nwith seasonable temperatures as sfc high pressure remains in \ncontrol over the Great Lakes region. While the ridge axis begins\nto shift more east from the Plains into the lower Ohio Valley \nduring the latter half of the week, the only noteworthy change \nwill be temperatures warming around 5 degrees above normal due \nto southerly return flow. Highs will range from the mid to \nupper 70s with lows struggling to dip below 50 degrees by the \nweekend. There are signs on some of the model guidance that a \ncold front will eventually impact the FA towards the middle of \nnext week as a potent trough ejects across the northern Plains.\nFor the foreseeable future, no precipitation is expected over \nthe next 7 days that would provide relief from the abnormally \ndry to moderate drought conditions.",
